#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lommel_t1

#% text
# `lommel_t1(mu, nu, z)` gives the modified Lommel function `t_(mu, nu)(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `t_(mu, nu)(z)` is the series `sum_k z^(mu + 1 + 2k)/prod_(j <= k) ((mu + 2j + 1)^2 - nu^2)`, the particular solution of `z^2 w'' + z w' - (z^2 + nu^2) w = z^(mu + 1)` (the Lommel `s` with `z^2` of the other sign, DLMF 11.9).

#% item
# When `mu + nu` or `mu - nu` is a negative odd integer a denominator vanishes and the value is `complex_infinity`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lommel_t1(-0.25, 2/3, 1)
#% output
#= 9.715613722586507

#% cell
n(lommel_t1(2, 0, 4), 30)
#% output
#= 13.484612772632462293130137197599015

#% cell
lommel_t1(7/3 + im, 2*im, 4.5 - im)
#% output
#= 20.986265403374414 - 2.1848635141216914im

#% cell
lommel_t1(1/2, 1/3, [0.5, 1.0, 1.5])
#% output
#= [0.1687303538790071, 0.5073486718147254, 1.0304890275918221]

#% cell
lommel_t1(2, 5, z)
#% output
#= complex_infinity

